TICVAI Resource Management
Board 1 — Resource Master Data & Configuration
Board Objective
Provide administrators with a centralized, intelligent backend workspace to create, classify, configure, 
organize, govern, and maintain every resource that can be used anywhere within the TICVAI platform.

TICVAI | RESOURCE MANAGEMENT
CONFIDENTIAL • 4
A resource may represent:
 Staff or personnel
 Venue
 Hall
 Room
 Stage
 Area
 Attraction space
 Equipment
 Asset
 Rental item
 Vehicle
 Locker
 Cabana
 Meeting room
 Stroller
 Towel
 AV equipment
 Sound or lighting equipment
 Any customer-defined resource type
The board must support resource reuse across ticketing, experiences, events, rentals, workforce scheduling, 
POS, mobile applications, and APIs.
Primary matrix coverage: 1.2.1, 1.2.2, 1.2.23–1.2.26, 1.2.44, 1.2.46, 1.2.72, 1.2.75, 1.2.77, 1.2.78.

