Screen 01 — Resource Management Command Center
Purpose
Provide administrators and operational managers with the main entry point for Resource Management and 
an instant overview of the organization's complete resource inventory.
Backend Configuration
The screen shall display configurable KPI widgets including:
 Total active resources
 Resources by type
 Resources by venue
 Available resources
 Assigned resources
 Reserved resources
 Resources under maintenance
 Suspended resources
 Retired resources
 Resources with expiring certifications
 Resources with unresolved configuration issues
 Recently created resources
 Recently modified resources
Administrators shall be able to filter the command center by:
 Tenant
 Business unit
 Country
 Venue
 Resource type
 Category
 Status
 Owner
 Department
 Tags
 Availability status
 Effective date
The screen shall provide quick actions for:
 Create resource
 Create resource type
 Create category
 Import resources
 Duplicate resource
 Assign resource to venue
 Create package
 Review configuration warnings

TICVAI | RESOURCE MANAGEMENT
CONFIDENTIAL • 6
An AI summary panel should highlight conditions such as:
 Unused resources
 Duplicate resources
 Missing attributes
 Resources approaching retirement
 Resources without venue assignments
 Unresolved resource dependencies
Business Rules
Dashboard information must respect the logged-in user's tenant, venue, department, and permission scope.
Users must only see resources they are authorized to manage.
Acceptance Condition
Authorized users can view the complete permitted resource estate, filter and search resources, identify 
configuration issues, and launch governed resource-management actions directly from the command center.
Screen 02 — Resource Type Configuration
Purpose
Allow administrators to define the different classes of resources supported by the organization without 
requiring software development.
Backend Configuration
Administrators shall be able to create configurable resource types such as:
 Staff
 Instructor
 Security personnel
 Venue
 Room
 Hall
 Area
 Cabana
 Equipment
 Asset
 Rental item
 Vehicle
 Locker
Each resource type shall support:
 Resource type code
 Resource type name
 Description
 Icon
 Display color
 Resource nature
 Physical / human / virtual classification
 Reservable yes/no

TICVAI | RESOURCE MANAGEMENT
CONFIDENTIAL • 7
 Rentable yes/no
 Capacity-controlled yes/no
 Schedule-controlled yes/no
 Inventory-controlled yes/no
 Staff qualification required yes/no
 Maintenance-controlled yes/no
 Check-in/check-out supported yes/no
 Deposit applicable yes/no
 Customer selectable yes/no
 API visible yes/no
Administrators shall determine which configuration sections are applicable to each resource type.
Example:
A Staff resource may require skills, certifications, shifts, breaks, and attendance.
A Cabana resource may require capacity, location, opening hours, price linkage, and availability.
A Towel resource may require inventory, checkout, deposit, return, and condition tracking.
Governance
Changes to resource-type definitions may require approval depending on tenant policy.
Existing resources must be evaluated when their resource type is changed.
Acceptance Condition
Administrators can create reusable resource types and define which operational capabilities and attributes 
apply to each type without code changes.
Screen 03 — Resource Category Management
Purpose
Provide a flexible classification structure beneath resource types so resources can be organized, searched, 
reported, and governed consistently.
Backend Configuration
Administrators shall create categories and subcategories such as:
 Equipment
 AV
 Lighting
 Sound
 Furniture
 Staff
 Instructor
 Operations
 Security
 Technical Crew
 Rental
 Towels
