Conditional attributes shall be supported.
Example:
If Resource Type = Vehicle, display vehicle registration and passenger capacity.
If Resource Type = Instructor, display skill level, languages, and qualifications.
Acceptance Condition
Administrators can extend resource records with reusable, validated, type-specific attributes without 
requiring application development.
Screen 06 — Resource Hierarchy & Parent–Child Relationships
Purpose
Represent physical and operational relationships between resources.
Backend Configuration
Administrators shall be able to create parent-child relationships such as:
Venue
→ Building
→ Floor
→ Hall
→ Room

TICVAI | RESOURCE MANAGEMENT
CONFIDENTIAL • 12
or:
AV System
→ Projector
→ Screen
→ Speakers
→ Microphones
The screen shall provide:
 Tree view
 Expand/collapse hierarchy
 Drag-and-drop organization
 Parent selection
 Child-resource assignment
 Relationship type
 Effective date
 Relationship priority
 Dependency indication
Supported relationship examples:
 Contains
 Belongs to
 Located in
 Operated by
 Supported by
 Part of
 Dedicated to
The system shall prevent:
 Circular hierarchies
 Invalid parent relationships
 Cross-tenant relationships without authorization
Operational Impact
Hierarchy may influence:
 Availability
 Capacity
 Maintenance
 Reporting
 Reservations
 Event allocation
Example:
If an entire hall is closed for maintenance, resources configured as dependent children may also become 
unavailable.
Acceptance Condition
Administrators can create and manage multi-level resource hierarchies, and the platform validates those 
relationships before they are used operationally.

