Screen 07 — Resource Dependency Rules
Purpose
Define operational relationships where one resource requires, depends upon, conflicts with, or influences 
another resource.
Backend Configuration
Administrators shall be able to configure dependencies such as:
 Requires
 Requires one of
 Requires all
 Conflicts with
 Cannot operate simultaneously
 Preferred with
 Substitute for
 Backup for
 Shares capacity with
Example:
Stage A
requires:
 Sound System A
 Lighting Rig A
Private Ski Lesson
requires:
 One instructor
 One training zone
Dependency rules shall support:
 Minimum quantity
 Maximum quantity
 Mandatory/optional
 Priority
 Effective dates
 Venue limitation
 Time overlap rules
 Availability dependency
 Capacity dependency
The system must evaluate dependencies before confirming assignments or reservations.
Conflict Detection
The system shall display:
 Missing dependencies
 Resource conflicts
 Circular dependency warnings
 Unavailable dependent resources

TICVAI | RESOURCE MANAGEMENT
CONFIDENTIAL • 14
Acceptance Condition
Administrators can define reusable dependency rules, and the system validates those dependencies before 
affected resources can be reserved or assigned.
