 Stage
 Sound equipment
 Lighting
 Technician
 Security
Administrators shall configure:
 Package code
 Package name
 Description
 Applicable venues
 Included resources
 Included resource types
 Required quantities
 Mandatory/optional components
 Substitute resources
 Allocation priority
 Effective dates
 Minimum/maximum duration
 Approval requirement
 Internal package cost
Packages should support:
 Fixed resources

TICVAI | RESOURCE MANAGEMENT
CONFIDENTIAL • 15
 Dynamic resources
 Skill-based staff resources
 Resource-type placeholders
Example:
Instead of assigning John Smith, the package may request:
1 × Technician with AV Level 2 certification.
The allocation engine can then select the most suitable available technician.
Acceptance Condition
Administrators can create reusable resource packages containing fixed or dynamically selected resources 
and use those packages later during experience, event, reservation, and operational allocation.
Screen 09 — Multi-Venue Resource Assignment
Purpose
Control where resources may operate and whether they can be shared across venues.
Backend Configuration
The screen shall support:
 Primary venue
 Secondary venues
 Shared resource pool
 Venue availability
 Department ownership
 Effective dates
 Travel/setup buffer
 Cross-venue booking permission
 Resource transfer requirement
 Transfer time
 Venue-specific restrictions
 Venue-specific cost
Example:
A portable projector may belong to Venue A but be shared with Venue B.
An instructor may work across several attractions or venues.
Administrators shall determine whether the resource is:
 Venue-exclusive
 Venue-shared
 Tenant-wide
 Temporary transfer
 Centrally pooled
Validation
The platform shall check for:
 Overlapping assignments
 Travel/setup time

TICVAI | RESOURCE MANAGEMENT
CONFIDENTIAL • 16
 Venue authorization
 Venue-specific qualification requirements
Acceptance Condition
Resources can be assigned to one or multiple venues under controlled rules, with conflicts and transfer 
constraints validated before operational allocation.
