Board 2 Shared Rules
All screens shall operate from a common real-time availability engine.
Changes made from one channel must immediately affect all authorized channels, including:
 Backend administration
 POS
 B2C
 B2B
 Employee App
 Event Management
 Ticketing
 API integrations
Resource availability must therefore never be maintained independently by each channel.
The platform shall support:
 Multi-tenant operation
 Multi-venue scheduling
 Time-zone awareness
 RBAC/PBAC
 Effective dating
 Approval workflows
 Real-time conflict detection
 API access
 Event-driven updates
 Immutable audit history
 AI recommendations
Board 2 End-to-End Outcome
Board 2 turns the resource master created in Board 1 into a live operational scheduling engine.
The end-to-end flow becomes:
Resource Availability Time Slot Search Reservation Conflict Validation Operational → → → → → →
Block Assignment Smart Reassignment Real-Time Calendar → → →
The most important design principle is that users should not have to think:
“Which resource should I assign?”
TICVAI should understand the requirement, availability, qualifications, dependencies and operational 
rules and present:
“These are the best resources available. This one is recommended.”
That is the experience that makes Resource Management feel like an AI-first operational platform 
rather than a traditional scheduling calendar.

