Board 4 End-to-End Outcome
After Board 4, TICVAI moves from knowing employee capabilities to actively managing the workforce.
The complete flow becomes:
Demand Staffing Requirement Roster Staff Assignment Coverage Validation → → → → →
Employee Request Attendance Compliance Labor Cost AI Optimization → → → →
TICVAI should therefore be able to tell an operations manager:
“Tomorrow you require 126 staff across three venues. You currently have 121 eligible 
employees scheduled. Five coverage gaps exist. I found qualified replacements for four of them
and one requires management action.”
And after optimization:
“All mandatory positions are covered. The proposed roster reduces overtime by 14 hours and 
projected labor cost by AED 2,100 while maintaining all qualification and compliance 
requirements.”
That is the intended intelligence level of the TICVAI Workforce Operations Engine.

