Screen 04 — Ticket Demand & Resource Capacity Mapping
Purpose
Connect ticket sales and participant quantity directly to resource requirements.
Capacity Models
Support:
 Fixed
One resource regardless of participant count.
Example:
1 Cabana per reservation.
 Ratio-Based
One resource per X participants.
Example:
1 Instructor per 8 participants.
 Tiered
1–8 participants 1 Instructor →
9–16 2 Instructors →
17–24 3 Instructors →
 Capacity-Based
Resource capacity determines maximum saleable inventory.
Example:
Training Area capacity = 30.
 Real-Time Calculation
TICVAI shall calculate:
Ticket Demand Participant Count Resource Demand Available Resource Capacity → → → →
Saleable Capacity
Example:
Session capacity: 40
Instructor ratio: 1:8
Available qualified instructors: 4
Maximum operational capacity:
32 participants
Even if the venue capacity is 40.
Capacity Protection
The system shall prevent ticket inventory from exceeding the capacity that can actually be supported 
by required resources unless an authorized oversell policy exists.
Acceptance Condition
