Board 8 — AI Decision Architecture
TICVAI should not create ten independent AI models for these screens.
Board 8 should operate through a common Resource Intelligence Layer consuming trusted 
operational data from the Resource Management domain.
The conceptual architecture is:
Operational Data
↓
Resource Digital Twin
↓
Availability & Eligibility Engine
↓
Demand Forecasting
↓
Optimization Engine
↓
AI Reasoning & Recommendation Layer
↓
Human Approval / Automation Policy
↓
Operational Execution
This allows the same intelligence to serve the backend, POS, Employee App, Event Management, and 
other authorized channels.
Board 8 — AI Confidence & Explainability
Every material AI recommendation should expose, where applicable:
 Recommendation
 Confidence
 Factors considered
 Mandatory constraints
 Alternatives
 Operational impact
 Financial impact
 Risks
 Data freshness
Example:
AI Recommendation — 96% Confidence
Transfer 4 instructors from Zone B to Zone A from 14:00–17:00.
Why:
✓ Zone A demand forecast +28%
✓ Zone B has forecast spare capacity

