Zone B Coverage: 118% 103% →
Board 8 — Human-in-the-Loop Governance
AI autonomy shall be configurable by action type.
Recommendation Only
AI proposes an action but cannot execute it.
User Confirmation
AI proposes and an authorized user confirms.
Approval Required
AI proposes, user submits, authorized approver approves.
Auto-Execute
Allowed only for explicitly approved low-risk scenarios.
Examples might include:
 Recommending resources — automatic
 Low-risk resource rebalancing — configurable
 Employee shift changes — approval
 Safety-critical staffing changes — mandatory approval
 Financially significant changes — approval
AI must never bypass:
 Safety rules
 Qualification requirements
 Certification requirements
 Capacity rules
 Legal/workforce rules
 Approval policies
 User permissions
Board 8 — Learning & Feedback
Where approved, TICVAI shall capture outcomes such as:
Recommendation Accepted / Rejected Actual Result → →
This may be used to evaluate and improve future recommendation quality.
Examples:
 Forecast accuracy
 Replacement success
 Staffing forecast accuracy
 Optimization savings achieved

