The employee should not have to search the application to determine what needs attention.
Board 9 — Mobile AI Copilot
The Resource AI layer from Board 8 should be available in a controlled form through the Employee 
App.
Employees may ask:
“Where is my next assignment?”
“Which equipment do I need?”
“Can I swap my Friday shift?”
“Who should I hand this radio to?”
Managers may ask:
“Who hasn't checked in?”
“Show me today's staffing gaps.”
“Find a replacement for Ahmed.”
The Copilot shall only return information and actions the logged-in user is permitted to access.
Board 9 — Offline-First Architecture
Because TICVAI may operate in attractions, stadiums, theme parks, event venues, and temporary 
event environments, selected Employee App capabilities should be designed to tolerate unstable 
connectivity.
The architecture should therefore support, where required:
Server State
↓
Encrypted Local Operational Cache
↓
Offline Action Queue
↓
Connectivity Restored
↓
Validation & Conflict Detection
↓
Server Synchronization
Offline support must never create uncontrolled duplicate assignments or conflicting resource states.

